# Breeches, Eager Pillager: "Whenever a Pirate you control attacks, choose one that hasn't been chosen this turn - Create a Treasure token; Target creature can't block
# this turn; Exile the top card of your library. You may play it this turn." (CR 508.1, 603.2c, 700.2) Turn 1 Bot1 casts Breeches (a Goblin Pirate) and a Goblin Tomb Raider
# (also a Pirate) with Black Lotus and two Moxen, and a non-Pirate Ornithopter. On turn 3 all three attack Bot2, which controls an Ornithopter: the two Pirates trigger the
# ability once each and the Ornithopter triggers nothing. The first trigger chooses the Treasure; choosing it again for the second trigger is refused, so the second takes
# "target creature can't block" aimed at Bot2's Ornithopter. Nothing blocks, so 3 + 2 + 0 combat damage reaches Bot2 (Raider 1+1 for the Mox), and the Treasure is Bot1's.

